  "edition": "2026-11-20",
  "intro": "Peak power leads this edition. Rajasthan told RERC that only about 10% of its evening exchange bids cleared in September; RERC let it buy Himachal hydro at Rs 15.50/kWh and take a single bidder's peak power at up to Rs 9.99/kWh. Tamil Nadu, which says it secured 15% to 25% of its peak bids even at the Rs 10 ceiling, has TNERC's approval to tender up to 3,200 MW a month for summer 2027. The longer-term answer is storage: CERC adopted Rs 6.27 to 6.28/kWh for 1,200 MW of four-hour evening supply from batteries in SECI's FDRE-VII, and TNERC approved 600 MW of solar with 1,800 MWh of storage at Rs 3.12/kWh. Developers should also note two hard lines: CERC will not extend the full ISTS waiver past 30 June 2026 even where transmission was late, and GERC would not stop a battery developer's bank guarantee over a West Asia force majeure claim.",
